#: levels/l3_church.gd:1031
msgid "Sermon Draft: Advent IV"
msgstr ""

#: levels/l3_church.gd:1032
msgid ""
"[b]SERMON — ADVENT IV (draft, unfinished)[/b]\n"
"\n"
"They ask us to give thanks for the jobs. For the mine, for the data centre, for the lithium that will make tomorrow cleaner. I have stood in this pulpit nineteen years and given thanks for worse.\n"
"\n"
"But I buried eleven men from the Lower Kettle in 2011, and nobody thanked them on the way down. [crossed out: The new people are polite. They sent the parish a fruit basket and a letter about community heat credits.]\n"
"\n"
"Tonight this is the only building in Kettle Falls with a wood stove, and sixty people came. I don't know what to say to them.\n"
"\n"
"[in pencil, below] Say nothing. Light the candles. Keep them awake. KEEP THEM AWAKE.\n"
"\n"
"[in a different hand] The singing started at three. It sounds like us. Ruth Kade stayed past midnight with the blankets. I told her to go home to the school. She said the lake was calling."
msgstr ""

#: levels/l3_church.gd:1033
msgid "Mom's Note"
msgstr ""

#: levels/l3_church.gd:1034
msgid ""
"[b]Elias —[/b]\n"
"\n"
"I know you'll come. You always said you were coming. I've stopped being angry about it.\n"
"\n"
"I'm going down to the mine tonight. Your father is calling me from the lake. I'm a nurse, Elias — I know what a fever dream sounds like, and I know this isn't one. It doesn't matter. It's his voice, and it says my name the way he said it in the kitchen.\n"
"\n"
"I came here to say goodbye to a few people. They were already singing. They let me through. I think they know me.\n"
"\n"
"June followed me out of the school. I sent her back. I don't think she went.\n"
"\n"
"If you find my rosary, keep it. If you find me, don't let me be the thing that's singing.\n"
"\n"
"— Mom"
msgstr ""

#: levels/l3_church.gd:1143
msgid "Burning barrels and flares keep the Rimebound back. Shops break their line of sight."
msgstr ""

#: levels/l3_church.gd:1154
msgid "Corvane Community Heat Credit"
msgstr ""

#: levels/l3_church.gd:1155
msgid ""
"[b]CORVANE SYSTEMS — Community Partnerships[/b]\n"
"\n"
"Dear Kettle Falls Neighbor,\n"
"\n"
"We are delighted to enrol your household in the [b]Community Heat Credit[/b]: $40 each month, applied automatically to your winter heating bill, for as long as MERIDIAN remains a proud member of the Kettle Falls community.\n"
"\n"
"Because MERIDIAN draws less cooling load in winter, we are able to share the benefits of our efficiency with you. Isn't that what neighbours do?\n"
"\n"
"[font_size=11]Credits are suspended during Grid Priority Events. A Grid Priority Event is declared at the sole discretion of the Operator.[/font_size]\n"
"\n"
"Warmly,\n"
"Brooke A. Lindahl\n"
"Director, Community Partnerships"
msgstr ""

#: levels/l3_church.gd:1160
msgid "Pharmacy Cold-Exposure Log"
msgstr ""

#: levels/l3_church.gd:1161
msgid ""
"[b]KETTLE FALLS PHARMACY — COLD EXPOSURE LOG[/b]\n"
"\n"
"Dec 18, 22:10 — M. Brandvold, 71. Core temp 91.4. Warmed up, refused to leave. Fell asleep in the chair.\n"
"\n"
"Dec 19, 03:40 — Three on cots. All asleep. They don't wake. They are not cold the way they should be. They are colder than that.\n"
"\n"
"Dec 19, 05:15 — Checked an airway. Frost inside the mouth. Not on the lips: inside. On the tongue, down the throat. Fine white needles, like a freezer shelf. I closed the mouth. It opened again.\n"
"\n"
"Dec 19, 06:00 — Whatever else you do, do not let them sleep.\n"
"\n"
"[i]— D.H.[/i]  (the sacristy key is on my lanyard, if Father Okafor sends anyone)"
msgstr ""

#: levels/l3_church.gd:1168
msgid "Cardboard Sign: Lindqvist Hardware"
msgstr ""

#: levels/l3_church.gd:1169
msgid ""
"[b](marker, on a flattened box)[/b]\n"
"\n"
"SPACE HEATERS — SOLD OUT (Tues)\n"
"ROCK SALT — SOLD OUT\n"
"PROPANE — 4 LEFT. KIDS AND OLD FIRST.\n"
"CASH — I DON'T WANT YOUR CASH.\n"
"\n"
"SHELLS: 12 LEFT. I'M KEEPING 2.\n"
"\n"
"Counted them from the roof. Eleven on Main at midnight. Nineteen by three. They don't run. They just come, like it's closing time and they're all headed for the same door.\n"
"\n"
"Gave the Halvorsen girl my last heater. Went back for the shotgun. If you're reading this it's behind the counter. It's yours. It's loud, and they listen to loud.\n"
"\n"
"— Don Lindqvist. Open since 1954. Still open."
msgstr ""

#: levels/l3_church.gd:1172
msgid "NOTICE — READ ME"
msgstr ""

#: levels/l3_church.gd:1173
msgid "Notice on the Church Door"
msgstr ""

#: levels/l3_church.gd:1174
msgid ""
"[b]ST. BRENDAN'S — NOTICE[/b]\n"
"\n"
"Services and warming hours are moved to the sacristy until the heat comes back. Please use the SIDE DOOR on the west wall. The front doors have frozen shut; do not force them. Those hinges are the oldest thing in Kettle Falls and I would like them to outlast me.\n"
"\n"
"The sacristy key is with Dolores Halloran at the pharmacy. She keeps it on her lanyard with the safe key; she has been helping with the elderly.\n"
"\n"
"Bring a blanket if you can spare one. Do not sleep in the pews.\n"
"\n"
"[i]— Fr. Emeka Okafor[/i]\n"
"\n"
"P.S. If you hear singing at night, it isn't us."
msgstr ""

